# Core Terraform Components

## Provider

A provider allows Terraform to communicate with external platforms.

Example:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}
```

The AWS Provider translates Terraform configuration into AWS API calls.

---

## Resources

Resources represent actual infrastructure.

Examples:

- VPC
- EC2
- S3 Bucket
- IAM Role
- EKS Cluster

Example:

```hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "state" {
  bucket = "my-tf-state"
}
```

---

## Variables

Variables make configurations reusable.

Example:

```hcl
variable "region" {
  default = "us-east-1"
}
```

Benefits:

- Reusability
- Cleaner code
- Environment-specific configuration

---

## Outputs

Outputs expose useful information after deployment.

Example:

```hcl
output "cluster_name" {
  value = aws_eks_cluster.main.name
}
```

Useful for:

- CI/CD pipelines
- Scripts
- Other Terraform modules

---

## Modules

Modules are reusable collections of Terraform resources.

Instead of writing everything in one file:

```
VPC

Subnets

Routes

Internet Gateway

NAT Gateway
```

All infrastructure can be grouped into:

```
modules/

vpc/

eks/

network/
```

Benefits:

- Reusable
- Easy maintenance
- Cleaner structure

